            <ArticleTitle>Prevention of post-herpetic neuralgia. Evaluation of treatment with oral prednisone, oral acyclovir, and radiotherapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>288-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effects of prednisone, oral acyclovir, and radiotherapy were compared with placebo in the prevention of post-herpetic neuralgia. No treatment used was able to prevent, with statistical significance, post-herpetic neuralgia, although prednisone and acyclovir showed some pain reduction in the acute phase. Radiotherapy was of no value in either the acute or post-herpetic phase.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
